  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Strong upper level ridging remains the\ndominant feature across northern and central Nevada. An upper\nlevel trough will skirt across southern Canada through the next\nday or two, resulting in breezy to locally windy conditions across\nthe area. Expect critical fire weather criteria to be reached\ntomorrow over portions of Elko county and have issued a red flag\nfor the afternoon. Other locales will continue to see quiet or\nelevated fire weather conditions. Though it may not feel like it,\na dry cold front marching across the area Sunday and Sunday night\nwill bring a few degrees of cooling Sunday. High temperatures will\ngenerally be in the 90s with lows in the 50s. \n\nThe upper ridge will be suppressed southward Monday and Tuesday in\nresponse to the aforementioned upper trough. This will bring\nanother couple of degrees of cooling Monday with dry conditions\npersisting. Highs will remain in the low to mid 90s with lows in\nthe 50s. Models are suggesting the upper ridge circulation moving\nwest on Tuesday with some slight warming, though temperatures over\nthe area will remain in the 90s. No precipitation is expected\nunder this feature and lows will be in the 50s.\n\nWednesday through Friday, the upper level ridge that brought us\nthe triple digit heat will consolidate and strengthen over this\ntime frame with more triple digit anticipated. HeatRisk will be at\nleast moderate with locations possibly needing heat headline\nproduct during the mid to latter portions of next week and will\nneed to keep watch. Otherwise, no precipitation is expected during\nthis time frame with many locations either surpassing the century\nmark or flirting with it by a a degree or two. Overnight lows will\nbe in the 50s and 60s. Occasional afternoon breezes to 20 mph are\npossible. Long term progs are showing the possibility of mid-level\nmoisture returning Saturday, but given all this heat, this will\nlead to isolated dry thunderstorms in central Nevada. Will need to\nkeep an eye on this as well.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Minor adjustments to the winds\nwere made to highlight the higher winds in northeast Nevada.\nOtherwise, no changes were made. Confidence in slight cooling is\nhigh for tomorrow and early next week. Confidence is also high in\nthe red flag conditions tomorrow for fire zone 470. Moderate\nconfidence exists for the warmup once again next week.",
